/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 49 0 R
/T (Built in 1930 on Abu Nuwas Street in central Baghdad, the House of Antiques is a traditional Baghdadi residence of approximately 500 square metres, consisting of two floors, 14 rooms, a traditional Baghdadi courtyard, and a rear garden.)
/E (Built in 1930 on Abu Nuwas Street in central Baghdad, the House of Antiques is a traditional Baghdadi residence of approximately 500 square metres, consisting of two floors, 14 rooms, a traditional Baghdadi courtyard, and a rear garden.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
74 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 49 0 R
/T (The house belongs to the Al-Almani family, a well-known Baghdadi family with a longstanding interest in antiques and works of art. Over the years, the house became home to a diverse collection of objects including copper, silver and wooden pieces, crystal, paintings, artworks, decorative objects and antiques from different periods and origins.)
/E (The house belongs to the Al-Almani family, a well-known Baghdadi family with a longstanding interest in antiques and works of art. Over the years, the house became home to a diverse collection of objects including copper, silver and wooden pieces, crystal, paintings, artworks, decorative objects and antiques from different periods and origins.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
