/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (Following 2004, amid the decline in tourism, international delegations and the wider circumstances Iraq was experiencing at the time, the House of Antiques ceased its activities and remained closed for many years.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (During this period, the building showed increasing signs of age and neglect. Moisture affected parts of the structure, sections of the walls and interior details deteriorated, and the rear garden lost much of its original character. A number of antiques, artworks and objects within the collection also required conservation and restoration.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
92 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (The Mismar Foundation for Arts & Sustainable Development adopted the revitalization of the House of Antiques with the aim of preserving its architectural and heritage identity while returning the building to active use without altering its original character.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (The restoration and rehabilitation process extended over approximately three years. Works included moisture treatment, restoration of damaged walls and architectural elements, rehabilitation of interior spaces, and the restoration of the rear garden as an essential part of the house experience.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
